      {
        "number": 13,
        "internalPageId": 14,
        "title": "Attending a party! Mum! Are we attending Lilly’s party? I still don’t know. Your dad is having a meeting at work that day. I see. Well, maybe we can go with aunt Melissa. She is going as far as I know. Uhm… if she is going, you can go with her then. I am waiting for your father even if we arrive late. Ok! What are we getting her as a present? Oh! When are we buying it? We are planning to go and buy something on Friday. Fine, I am going with you, can I? Totally, we are leaving at 6:00pm. Oh! I am not getting you anything. Huh! I am staying at home then.",
        "visibleTexts": [
          "Attending a party! Mum! Are we attending Lilly’s party? I still don’t know. Your dad is having a meeting at work that day. I see. Well, maybe we can go with aunt Melissa. She is going as far as I know. Uhm… if she is going, you can go with her then. I am waiting for your father even if we arrive late. Ok! What are we getting her as a present? Oh! When are we buying it? We are planning to go and buy something on Friday. Fine, I am going with you, can I? Totally, we are leaving at 6:00pm. Oh! I am not getting you anything. Huh! I am staying at home then.",
          "C. Read the following dialogue and state if the sentences are true (T) or false (F). After that, read the dialogue with your teacher.",
          "1. Lilly is having a party. (T) (F) 2. They are attending for sure. (T) (F) 3. They are going with aunt Melissa. (T) (F) 4. Mum is waiting for dad to attend the party. (T) (F)",
